# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Cargo local config (dev-only: disables sccache wrapper)
.cargo/config.toml

# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock IS TRACKED, deliberately. It was ignored from the root commit
# onward, listed above under "build artifacts", which it is not: it is the
# record of which dependency versions a build actually used. This workspace
# ships a binary (batchalign3, installed across the fleet from GitHub
# Releases), and Cargo's guidance is to commit the lockfile for anything that
# produces one. Without it, the same source commit resolves a different
# dependency graph on different days, so `batchalign3 version` identifies the
# source and not the binary.

